<div class="prose prose-lg max-w-3xl mx-auto">

<p class="lead text-xl text-gray-600 mb-8">
The Nigerian tech services market doesn't have a capability gap. It has an <strong>accountability gap</strong>.
</p>

<p>Every burned founder knows the pattern. You pay a deposit. The vendor ghosts. The system is abandoned in six months. The code is written so poorly that <em>no other developer wants to touch it</em>. You've lost money, looked stupid, and you're left with a codebase that's effectively radioactive.</p>

<p>This isn't vibes. It's documented.</p>

</div>

<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">

<section class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8">
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">The evidence nobody talks about</h2>

<div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-6">
<dl class="space-y-3">
<dt class="font-semibold text-gray-900"><span class="text-primary">Businessday NG</span></dt>
<dd class="text-gray-600">"The accountability gap is one of the defining problems of the Nigerian tech services market." Prescribed cure: milestone payments tied to demonstrable deliverables, code/credential ownership established before a line is written.</dd>

<dt class="font-semibold text-gray-900"><span class="text-primary">Zikoko</span></dt>
<dd class="text-gray-600">Founder post-mortem: 3 developers, 3 failed attempts, millions lost. Key line: <em>"No other developer wanted to touch his code."</em> Code hostage-taking is a real, felt fear.</dd>

<dt class="font-semibold text-gray-900"><span class="textprimary">planetweb.ng</span></dt>
<dd class="text-gray-600">Lagos logistics company. ₦12M. 8 months. Abandoned. Rebuilding was cheaper than fixing.</dd>

<dt class="font-semibold text-gray-900"><span class="text-primary">The Gnar (US dev shop)</span></dt>
<dd class="text-gray-600">Differentiation = "make the claim checkable instead of claimed." Bug-free warranty, production code in week one, named packages. <em>"Find the claim a competitor would be afraid to guarantee, then guarantee it."</em></dd>
</dl>
</section>

<section class="bg-primary text-white rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8">
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Our position: <span class="text-yellow-300">"The studio you can audit."</span></h2>

<p class="text-primary-100 text-lg mb-6"><strong>We build software you can fire us from.</strong></p>

<p class="text-primary-100">That's the mind-capture hook. It's a paradox — pattern-interrupt in a feed of identical AI claims — and it's the exact inverse of every burned buyer's experience. The enemy isn't a competitor by name. It's the <em>pattern</em> every burned buyer recognizes instantly: the ghosting developer.</p>

