<section class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8">
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Why this works (sales psychology, not marketing fluff)</h2>

<div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-sm">
<div>
<h3 class="font-semibold text-yellow-300 mb-2">Loss aversion > feature gain</h3>
<p class="text-gray-300">Buyers don't ask "can they build it?" They ask "will I lose my money and look stupid?" We sell against the fear with verifiable structure.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="font-semibold text-yellow-300 mb-2">Specificity = credibility</h3>
<p class="text-gray-300">"17 production tools," "₦150k–₦400k," "day 14 demo or no bill," "your repo from commit #1." Vague claims don't convert; specific, checkable ones do.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="font-semibold text-yellow-300 mb-2">Guarantee competitors fear</h3>
<p class="text-gray-300">"Demo at day 14 or the milestone isn't billed." "Your repo, your credentials." No agency that ghosts can copy this without actually delivering.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h3 class="font-semibold text-yellow-300 mb-2">The "fire us" paradox</h3>
<p class="text-gray-300">We build so you can leave. Leaving is never needed precisely because leaving is always possible. That's the hook that earns attention in a feed of identical AI claims.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">Honest risks (we don't hide them)</h2>

<ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-600">
<li><strong>The guarantee is a delivery obligation.</strong> 14-day scope must stay ruthlessly small (one workflow, one dashboard). Over-scoping the pilot turns the campaign into the exact failure it attacks.</li>
<li><strong>Every public claim must match real system output.</strong> Our <a href="/proof" class="text-primary hover:underline">Proof Page</a> shows only real telemetry — no invented uptime, no staged screenshots, no mocked numbers.</li>
<li><strong>"Fire us" requires genuinely clean docs.</strong> Handover pack must be a real artifact from day 1, not a promise.</li>
<li><strong>Organic-first, zero ad spend.</strong> Founder-led LinkedIn, WhatsApp network, SEO targeting the exact Businessday search intent. No paid acquisition budget.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8">
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">The smallest experiment (running now)</h2>

<p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">We published three assets in two weeks:</p>

<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3 text-gray-600 mb-6">
<li><a href="/proof" class="text-primary hover:underline font-medium">/proof</a> — Live automation telemetry (nurture stats, 17 tools, deploy history, architecture)</li>
<li><a href="/14" class="text-primary hover:underline font-medium">/14</a> — 14-Day Proof offer, pricing tiers, FAQ, deliverables</li>
<li><a href="/labs/website-rater" class="text-primary hover:underline font-medium">Website Rater bridge</a> — "Send Me the Fix Plan" now routes to the pilot offer</li>
</ol>

<p class="text-gray-600 mb-4"><strong>Validate if:</strong> ≥5 pilot inquiries or ≥2 paid pilots in 30 days.</p>
<p class="text-gray-600"><strong>Kill/pivot if:</strong> Traffic clicks but zero inquiries after 30 days → the fear is real but the offer framing is wrong. Test price/scope before abandoning the position.</p>
</section>

<section class="text-center py-12">
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">You've been burned. We built the antidote.</h2>
<p class="text-gray-600 text-lg mb-8 max-w-xl mx-auto">No vague proposals. No hostage code. No ghosting. A working slice of your product in 14 days — in your repo, on your infra, demo at day 14 or the milestone isn't billed.</p>
